The traceplots actually do not look as bad as the divergence diagnostics would suggest. After looking at the posterior means, it looks like the problem is related to sampling of the non-decision time and starting point parameters.

Particularly, the non-decision time is piled up against 0, which suggests that you have many RTs near 0 in your data. Is that the case? It is a bit hard to tell by looking at the poster. If so, it may be useful to discard any trials where the RT is below a certain threshold.

If that does not solve any problems, we may be able to work something out by constraining the lower bound of the non-decision time to your minimum RT—this is done with the diffusion model, but not the LBA (which the Stan code is adapted from Annis, Miller, & Palmeri, 2016).

Best,
Nate
