Stan model 'choiceRT_lba_priors' does not contain samples.

Stan model 'choiceRT_lba_priors' does not contain samples.

I tried both with inits set at random and fixed.

Additionally - I'm not sure what do you mean by processing before stimuli are presented. It would seem to me that as long as the stimuli are counterbalanced (participant has no way of predicting which pair of stimuli will appear , nor whether his preferred stimulus is more likely to show on left or right side of the screen) then he can't exhibit a bias towards a particular stimulus before  presentation (unless we assume precognition :) ). Or do you mean something else?

On a side note - I am using LBA specifically because the analysis of qualitative features of the data indicates that classical DDM cannot fit this dataset. By 'classical' I mean preserving the assumption that threshold shouldn't change between conditions, when those are intermixed (Ratcliff & Smith 2004). The problem is that drift rate defined as relative difference in evidence cannot lead to both a) faster responses in condition A vs B and b) the same proportion of choices in A  & B. Independent drift rates for each accumulator should be able to resolve this problem. But, maybe LBA has different problem which I cannot pinpoint.

Best,
Wojciech

