No need to apologize! It's a rather confusing problem...

Let me just start that the later model (with extra long non-decision time) was a fluke due to a data error. After fixing it we are back to square 1 - the model consistently estimates unrealistically fast non-dec times. 2 new models I run:

1. Increasing adapt_delta to .975 and constricting the priors a bit almost eliminated divergent transitions (only 4 out of 5000 samples), but the estimations for non-decision time still are impossibly short:
