> Counterbalancing should alleviate some of those problems, but what I mean is that in value-based tasks, the participants likely have an idea of which stimuli they prefer within each pair. This could potentially lead to some difficulties in identifying the separate effects of the non-decision time, starting point, and/or decision threshold. That said, I would expect this to show up in the pairs plots as correlation between parameters, which we did not see (at least in the hyper-parameters). It is possible that there is a trade-off at the individual subject level, though—could you post some pairs plots of one or two of the individual subjects?
